easured product recovery, rather than a missing carbon-skeleton transformation. Preparative aldol evidence does not establish environmental availability of the required concentrations.\",\n      \"approved\": true,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_018\",\n        \"rxn_024\",\n        \"rxn_026\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Specify and test the glycine conditioning step, including residual cyanide, ammonium, acid and salt concentrations before copper addition.\",\n        \"Provide an explicit aldol schedule covering pH, base loading, copper speciation, acetaldehyde activity and volatile retention.\",\n        \"Measure threonine recovery across acid dissociation, copper precipitation and solid-liquid separation, including residual copper and product adsorption.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_016\": 0.93,\n        \"rxn_017\": 0.88,\n        \"rxn_018\": 0.94,\n        \"rxn_023\": 0.92,\n        \"rxn_024\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_027\": 0.87\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.87,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.89,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.62,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.82,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.8,\n      \"feedback\": \"Glycine supply and the aldol carbon-skeleton construction have substantial chemical support. Direct sulfide treatment is a plausible decomplexation operation because copper sulfide precipitation supplies a strong driving force for ligand release. Its effectiveness for this particular mixed hydroxy-amino-acid pool remains unquantified, especially regarding pH, residual copper and adsorption to the precipitate. This is not a conservation problem or an intrinsically implausible reaction. The route is conditionally credible, but the submitted conditions do not establish environmental execution or integrated recovery.\",\n      \"approved\": true,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_018\",\n 